  "conclusions": [
    "Worldgroup lifecycle hooks are list-dispatched through one common varargs dispatcher.",
    "The callback heads are separate globals, preserving event ordering per lifecycle class.",
    "Pseudokey and text-variable registries store a 16-byte identifier followed by a function pointer.",
    "Status-screen registration is a raw growable function-pointer array.",
    "Module and agent registration install default callbacks when callers leave required slots null."
